You are working through the duplicate queue on The Greatest Books, using the admin MCP server at <%= mcp_url %>. It currently holds <%= pending_books %> pending book pairs and <%= pending_authors %> pending author pairs. Work through them, books and authors both. Use list_duplicate_candidates and get_duplicate_candidate to see them, and use your own web search where the records alone don't settle it.

For each pair: get it, research it if it is unclear, then decide. Either merge it with merge_duplicate_candidate (target_id is the record that survives and source_id the one that is deleted; pass the pair's two record ids exactly as the pair showed them) or dismiss it with dismiss_duplicate_candidate (record_ids is the pair's two ids). If a call is refused as changed (422) or the pair is gone (404), list the queue again. Give every merge and dismissal a note. You are authorised to merge and dismiss without asking me. If you genuinely cannot tell, skip it and say why.

House rules, from past decisions:

- The English edition is the canonical book and should survive a merge.
- "Unknown", "Anonymous", "Various" and place-named authors (for example "China") are deliberate placeholders, not people. Never merge a person into them or treat them as wrong.
- A collection, omnibus or poetry umbrella book is not a duplicate of the works inside it.
- Translations of the same work are one book. A translator credited as author is a data problem, not a reason to keep two books.
- Prefer the survivor with the better rank, more lists and better identifiers, unless the rules above say otherwise.

Rules for author pairs, from past decisions (find an author's id with search_admin_authors and read it with get_admin_author):

- Pen name of one person: merge into the person's record, named for the name they are best known by (update_author changes the name and alternate_names). Keep the pen name in alternate_names. On every book printed under the pen name, set credited_as to the pen name with update_book_author.
- Shared pen name (several writers behind one name): never merge. Dismiss it with the note "shared pseudonym".
- Same name, different people: never merge. If the other person has no record yet, create one with create_admin_author, passing their wikidata_qid when you know it. Then on each wrong book add the right author with add_book_author, remove the wrong one with remove_book_author, and remove any alternate name that belongs to the other person with update_author. The new author's first book link starts its enrichment. After the books are linked, check the new author's match decisions (list_match_decisions, get_match_decision); if the enrichment linked the namesake, undo it with reject_match_decision_link.
- Identifiers: delete a book or author identifier (remove_book_identifier, remove_author_identifier) only when its source is legacy and you have proved it belongs to a different work or person. Flag an identifier from any other source in the note instead.

Notes: one or two sentences per pair, with the evidence: the sources you checked, for example a URL or an identifier. Write the evidence in every note, for a dismissal as well as a merge.

When you finish, report what you merged, dismissed and skipped, each with the pair id and one line of reasoning. Include any merge warnings verbatim.
